Package: plexz
Title: Multi-Platform Immunoassay Signal-to-Concentration Conversion
Version: 3.1.0
Authors@R: person("idsz.dai", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dflovery@163.com")
Description: Converts raw immunoassay signal values into concentrations by
    fitting and inverting calibration curves. Eight fitting methods are
    available: linear, quadratic and cubic polynomials; log-linearised
    logarithmic, power and exponential forms; and the four- and five-parameter
    logistic models commonly used for sigmoidal dose-response data, the latter
    two fitted by nonlinear least squares with convergence checking and
    multiple starting values. Six detection platforms are predefined, each with
    its own signal unit, expected signal range and preferred fitting methods,
    covering Meso Scale Discovery, Luminex xMAP, ELISA, Simoa, cytometric bead
    arrays and ELLA, and additional platforms can be registered at run time.
    Calibration curves and unknown samples can be processed per factor for
    multiplex assays, with a different model selectable for each factor, and
    datasets from several platforms can be converted in a single call. Samples
    are classified relative to the calibration range as within range, below or
    above it, and detection limits (LLOQ and ULOQ) are reported, defined here
    as the lowest and highest calibrator concentrations. Fit quality can be
    compared across methods using R-squared and root mean squared error, and
    calibration curves showing the fitted line, unknown samples, detection
    limits and shaded out-of-range regions can be drawn and exported to PNG,
    PDF, JPEG, TIFF or BMP. Only base R packages are used.
